import Cryptificate.Grain.Generator

/-!
# Published constants the generator reproduces

Round constants copied from three public implementations, each produced by the Grain procedure,
and `#guard` checks that `Grain.poseidon2Constants` reproduces them. `#guard` evaluates with the
compiled code, not the kernel: these are tests of the transcription's faithfulness, not part of
any certificate. (`Grain.bn254_reference` checks the BN254 instance in the kernel.)

* HorizenLabs/poseidon2 at commit `055bde3f4782731ba5f5ce5888a440a94327eaf3`,
  `plain_implementations/src/poseidon2/poseidon2_instance_babybear.rs` (`RC16`, BabyBear,
  `t = 16`, `R_F = 8`, `R_P = 13`, `x^7`) and `poseidon2_instance_goldilocks.rs` (`RC8`,
  Goldilocks, `t = 8`, `R_F = 8`, `R_P = 22`, `x^7`): the output of `poseidon2_rust_params.sage`,
  one row per round, partial rounds `[c, 0, …, 0]`.
* Plonky3 at commit `0d803737b681774186cd283b1fd2d8e493655c82`, `koala-bear/src/poseidon2.rs`
  (`KOALABEAR_POSEIDON2_RC_16_EXTERNAL_INITIAL`, `…_INTERNAL`, `…_EXTERNAL_FINAL`; KoalaBear,
  `t = 16`, `R_F = 8`, `R_P = 20`, `x^3`): the same constants split into the first four full
  rounds, one constant per partial round and the last four full rounds. Plonky3 documents them as
  "Generated by the Grain LFSR with parameters: field_type=1, alpha=3 (exp_flag=0), n=31, t=16,
  R_F=8, R_P=20".

The Plonky3 layout is turned into the Poseidon2 one by padding each partial-round constant with
`t - 1` zeros (`Grain.fromSplit`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace Cryptificate.Grain.Vectors

